  "description": "A sorted, in-memory IDictionary<TKey, TValue> for .NET backed by a B+ tree, built for collections that are loaded at runtime and then queried repeatedly.\n\nAt 450,000 keys it loads roughly 100x faster than SortedList while using the same memory, and beats SortedDictionary on load time, memory, exact lookup and range search alike. Values live at the leaf level and leaves are kept in key order, so inserts stay local to one node and range queries become a forward walk over a sorted, indexable leaf list instead of one lookup per key.",
  "id": "SP.BPlusTreeCollection",
